WEBVTT

00:00.640 --> 00:02.520
<b>SEPTEMBER 23, A.D. 2096</b>

00:03.140 --> 00:05.730
<b>Big Bro Tatsuya, Ms. Miyuki...</b>

00:07.150 --> 00:09.150
<b>It's been a long time.</b>

00:09.400 --> 00:11.030
<b>Since the Nine Schools Competition, right?</b>

00:11.400 --> 00:13.780
<b>You really made your mark
in that tournament.</b>

00:13.780 --> 00:16.070
<b>We're humbled to receive such praise.</b>

00:16.530 --> 00:19.450
<b>So, for you two to go out of your way
and come all the way here...</b>

00:19.870 --> 00:21.950
<b>what did you want to discuss?</b>

00:21.950 --> 00:23.580
<b>Uh, right!</b>

00:25.210 --> 00:28.340
<b>I was personally instructed
to bring you this by the head.</b>

00:38.800 --> 00:41.100
<b>Fumiya, do you know...</b>

00:41.470 --> 00:42.890
<b>what's written in here?</b>

00:43.350 --> 00:45.060
<b>Yes, I do.</b>

00:45.060 --> 00:46.520
<b>I see.</b>

00:46.980 --> 00:52.280
<b>This is a request for our cooperation
in apprehending Gongjin Zhou.</b>

00:55.450 --> 01:00.240
<b>Brother, why would our aunt
request such a thing of us?</b>

01:00.240 --> 01:01.620
<b>Regarding that...</b>

01:01.950 --> 01:04.750
<b>I have been entrusted
with a message from her.</b>

01:05.080 --> 01:09.210
<b>She says that if you should decline
this request, she won't have any objections.</b>

01:09.540 --> 01:11.710
<b>Aunt Maya actually said such a thing?</b>

01:12.380 --> 01:16.430
<b>Fumiya, let our aunt know
that we've accepted her request.</b>

01:16.760 --> 01:18.760
<b>I'll be sure to relay that to her.</b>

01:18.760 --> 01:22.430
<b>Now then, could you tell us
what you've discovered so far?</b>

01:22.430 --> 01:23.180
<b>Sure.</b>

01:23.560 --> 01:26.770
<b>About Gongjin Zhou, after fleeing Yokohama...</b>

01:26.770 --> 01:29.900
<b>he headed west by sea, arriving in Ise.</b>

01:29.900 --> 01:33.230
<b>After that, though at one point,
he was captured on the Great Biwa Lake Bridge,</b>

01:33.230 --> 01:34.940
<b>he managed to get away.</b>

01:35.240 --> 01:38.450
<b>Currently, we're searching
the Ohara area in Kyoto.</b>

01:38.740 --> 01:40.830
<b>Any information on his supporters?</b>

01:41.120 --> 01:45.750
<b>The Traditionalists, an organization of Ancient Magic
users in opposition with the families of the number Nine,</b>

01:45.370 --> 01:48.330
<b>THE TRADITIONALISTS</b>

01:45.750 --> 01:48.330
<b>are thought to be aiding
his escape efforts.</b>

01:48.670 --> 01:50.460
<b>The Traditionalists, huh?</b>

01:50.460 --> 01:53.340
<b>I've heard a little about them
from Master Yakumo.</b>

01:53.340 --> 01:56.840
<b>Not only have they been gathering
outcast Ancient Magic users here in Japan,</b>

01:56.840 --> 01:59.930
<b>but they've also been looking
to bolster the organization...</b>

01:59.930 --> 02:02.180
<b>by sheltering tacticians
who've defected from the Continent.</b>

02:03.680 --> 02:06.980
<b>Apparently, the Kudous also took in
some of those tacticians...</b>

02:06.980 --> 02:09.850
<b>but is it possible
that they're aiding him, as well?</b>

02:09.850 --> 02:11.440
<b>No need to worry about that.</b>

02:11.730 --> 02:16.400
<b>Right after escaping from Yokohama,
Gongjin Zhou fled the former Ninth Institute...</b>

02:16.400 --> 02:18.740
<b>and joined the Traditionalists.</b>

02:19.320 --> 02:20.490
<b>Thanks.</b>

02:20.490 --> 02:22.240
<b>That helps a lot.</b>

04:01.050 --> 04:06.390
<b>It seems like our aunt's request really
is just about helping to capture Gongjin Zhou.</b>

04:06.720 --> 04:12.520
<b>Why do you suppose she opted for a request
rather than an order just this one time?</b>

04:12.850 --> 04:18.230
<b>You two probably don't know this,
but our aunt's commands are actually low-priority.</b>

04:18.860 --> 04:22.610
<b>It goes without saying that keeping
Miyuki safe is the top priority,</b>

04:22.610 --> 04:26.530
<b>but the next highest are the missions
of the Independent Magic-Equipped Battalion.</b>

04:26.820 --> 04:30.290
<b>Our aunt's authority to issue commands
follows at number three.</b>

04:30.870 --> 04:32.790
<b>I didn't know that.</b>

04:32.790 --> 04:37.130
<b>But until now, whenever she instructed me
to carry out a mission,</b>

04:37.130 --> 04:39.750
<b>she's always done it
in the form of a command.</b>

04:39.750 --> 04:41.460
<b>That was normal.</b>

04:44.010 --> 04:48.800
<b>If she's using extraordinary methods,
she must have an extraordinary reason.</b>

04:49.430 --> 04:53.310
<b>Does that mean that this mission
is particularly dangerous?</b>

04:53.600 --> 04:56.480
<b>It's someone who seriously wounded
the head of the Kuroba Family...</b>

04:56.480 --> 04:59.940
<b>and is even now fleeing from
the Yotsubas' attempts to track him down.</b>

05:00.270 --> 05:04.200
<b>Neither capturing him nor getting rid of him
will be an easy task.</b>

05:06.570 --> 05:08.570
<b>Will there be a battle?</b>

05:09.490 --> 05:12.240
<b>Miyuki, don't give me that look.</b>

05:12.240 --> 05:14.410
<b>It's not as if I'm going to take him on alone.</b>

05:14.710 --> 05:20.210
<b>Since what she's seeking of me is most likely
to block our target's escape route.</b>

05:20.210 --> 05:21.840
<b>Is that right?</b>

05:22.300 --> 05:26.510
<b>But from time to time,
I'll probably have to leave the house.</b>

05:27.590 --> 05:29.300
<b>When that happens, Minami...</b>

05:29.300 --> 05:31.100
<b>I want you to protect Miyuki.</b>

05:31.100 --> 05:32.600
<b>Oh! Right!</b>

05:33.180 --> 05:36.690
<b>In the Yotsubas' eyes,
you're Miyuki's guardian.</b>

05:36.690 --> 05:42.110
<b>But for me, you're more than that.
You're one of the few magicians that I can trust.</b>

05:42.690 --> 05:46.110
<b>When I'm not at home,
I'm counting on you to look after Miyuki.</b>

05:47.150 --> 05:49.110
<b>Please leave it to me!</b>

05:49.240 --> 05:51.370
<b>SEPTEMBER 24, A.D. 2096</b>

05:51.660 --> 05:54.120
<b>Come to think of it,
isn't it about time to elect our chairman?</b>

05:54.500 --> 05:58.250
<b>Last year, Ms. Miyuki was first
while you came in third, Tatsuya.</b>

05:58.250 --> 05:59.500
<b>Are you not running this year?</b>

05:59.960 --> 06:03.750
<b>Stop joking around. I never even signed up
to be a candidate last year, either.</b>

06:04.130 --> 06:06.010
<b>Then, what about the Thesis Competition?</b>

06:06.300 --> 06:08.550
<b>Hasn't anyone asked for your support?</b>

06:08.550 --> 06:10.640
<b>As of now, no one's asked me yet.</b>

06:11.100 --> 06:16.520
<b>Needless to say, I'll help if I'm asked to,
but I don't think I'm in the running this time.</b>

06:16.810 --> 06:18.770
<b>What? But why?</b>

06:18.770 --> 06:21.150
<b>Because it's going to be held
in Kyoto this year.</b>

06:21.690 --> 06:25.440
<b>The Thesis Competition is held
alternately in Yokohoma and Kyoto...</b>

06:25.440 --> 06:28.780
<b>but the terms of evaluation
differs depending on the venue.</b>

06:29.450 --> 06:32.780
<b>In Yokohama, they rate
technological themes higher...</b>

06:33.120 --> 06:37.790
<b>whereas in Kyoto, they're said
to favor purely theoretical themes.</b>

06:38.120 --> 06:42.290
<b>I see. So, you wouldn't be able
to make the most of your specialties, Tatsuya.</b>

06:42.840 --> 06:45.300
<b>Well, that's basically it.</b>

06:45.670 --> 06:47.300
<b>SEPTEMBER 29, A.D. 2096</b>

06:47.590 --> 06:50.300
<b><i>Hello? Tatsuya? This is Fujibayashi.</i></b>

06:50.890 --> 06:53.300
<b>Sorry to bother you at this hour.</b>

06:53.680 --> 06:57.560
<b><i>It's unusual for you
to be calling me, Tatsuya.</i></b>

06:57.560 --> 06:58.680
<b><i>What's going on?</i></b>

06:59.310 --> 07:02.940
<b>The thing is, I'd like to request
something of General Kudou.</b>

07:03.900 --> 07:04.940
<b>My grandfather?</b>

07:05.360 --> 07:10.820
<b>Yes. I'm not asking you as Lt. Fujibayashi,
who's also the Battalions' second-in-command...</b>

07:11.160 --> 07:14.240
<b>but as a daughter of the Fujibayashi Family.</b>

07:14.870 --> 07:18.330
<b>I'd like you to set up a private meeting
between His Excellency and myself.</b>

07:18.910 --> 07:20.660
<b><i>"Private"...</i></b>

07:20.660 --> 07:22.710
<b><i>meaning it's related to a Yotsuba task?</i></b>

07:23.130 --> 07:23.920
<b>That's correct.</b>

07:26.380 --> 07:28.920
<b><i>Would you mind telling me
what kind of job it is?</i></b>

07:29.380 --> 07:34.140
<b>To find and capture a tactician
named Gongjin Zhou.</b>

07:34.140 --> 07:35.550
<b><i>I see.</i></b>

07:35.550 --> 07:39.180
<b><i>And I understand why the Yotsubas
would want to ask for my grandfather's help.</i></b>

07:39.810 --> 07:41.020
<b>So...</b>

07:41.020 --> 07:44.060
<b><i>Yes. I'll ask my grandfather
when he can schedule it.</i></b>

07:44.060 --> 07:45.900
<b>Thank you very much.</b>

07:51.570 --> 07:54.030
<b>Brother, may I come in?</b>

07:54.700 --> 07:56.950
<b>Sure, it's all right.</b>

08:00.290 --> 08:04.290
<b>Would you mind my asking
who it was that you were calling?</b>

08:05.380 --> 08:07.170
<b>First Lt. Fujibayashi.</b>

08:07.460 --> 08:11.920
<b>Brother, are you going to seek help from
the Independent Magic-Equipped Battalion?</b>

08:12.510 --> 08:17.180
<b>No. I asked Ms. Fujibayashi to act as a mediator
between myself and General Kudou.</b>

08:17.510 --> 08:19.430
<b>Isn't that risky?</b>

08:19.430 --> 08:22.940
<b>Aren't all communications
with the battalion being censored?</b>

08:23.350 --> 08:24.940
<b>It should be fine.</b>

08:24.940 --> 08:28.070
<b>It was the lieutenant's private line
that I just called.</b>

08:28.610 --> 08:34.570
<b>It would be impossible to eavesdrop on a line
that the Electron Sorceress is using for private use.</b>

08:35.360 --> 08:37.070
<b>Is that right?</b>

08:37.700 --> 08:41.080
<b>Ms. Fujibayashi's private
phone number, did you say?</b>

08:41.950 --> 08:43.330
<b>Brother...</b>

08:43.330 --> 08:45.580
<b>Where did you acquire that number?</b>

08:57.140 --> 09:00.390
<b><i>A Compound-Form?
No, is it a synthetic spirit?</i></b>

09:00.970 --> 09:03.020
<b><i>Analyzing its compositional data.</i></b>

09:03.520 --> 09:05.060
<b><i>Disassembly... activate.</i></b>

09:08.060 --> 09:10.230
<b>Brother, what on earth was that?</b>

09:10.230 --> 09:11.440
<b>Right.</b>

09:11.440 --> 09:14.200
<b>A synthetic spirit
was lurking around our home.</b>

09:14.200 --> 09:17.070
<b>Probably due to that job request
we got the other day.</b>

09:17.570 --> 09:20.700
<b>Is that Gongjin Zhou person behind this?</b>

09:21.120 --> 09:25.500
<b>It's probably the work of one of his
subordinates or the people sheltering him.</b>

09:25.830 --> 09:27.960
<b>So, Fumiya and Ayako were being followed?</b>

09:28.630 --> 09:32.300
<b>Surely not! Ayako and Fumiya
wouldn't let anyone track them!</b>

09:32.300 --> 09:34.090
<b>It's probably deliberate.</b>

09:34.090 --> 09:37.840
<b>Are you saying that those two
guided the enemy here on purpose?</b>

09:41.850 --> 09:44.850
<b>Fumiya, are you disgruntled about this job?</b>

09:45.770 --> 09:48.230
<b>I don't have a problem
with the mission itself.</b>

09:48.730 --> 09:51.230
<b>So, it's the conditions you were given
that you don't like.</b>

09:51.650 --> 09:53.230
<b>Well, of course!</b>

09:53.230 --> 09:56.860
<b>Knowing that we're being followed
but not being able to do anything about it!</b>

09:56.860 --> 10:00.990
<b>I can never look Big Bro Tatsuya
in the eye again!</b>

10:01.530 --> 10:04.660
<b>We'll never know the truth
unless we ask them,</b>

10:04.660 --> 10:08.370
<b>but our aunt may be planning
to use me as a decoy.</b>

10:08.710 --> 10:09.750
<b>No way!</b>

10:09.750 --> 10:10.880
<b>Don't be angry.</b>

10:11.460 --> 10:12.840
<b>But...</b>

10:12.840 --> 10:16.130
<b>Anyway, using me as a decoy
is the sensible thing to do.</b>

10:16.510 --> 10:19.680
<b>Since ultimately, I won't sustain
any injuries as a tactical ploy,</b>

10:19.680 --> 10:23.260
<b>it's not wrong to put me
in the direct line of fire.</b>

10:23.260 --> 10:24.270
<b>Brother!</b>

10:26.020 --> 10:30.310
<b>Please don't speak so disparagingly
of your own safety!</b>

10:30.310 --> 10:34.400
<b>It's not a matter of simply not dying,
of not sustaining any lasting wounds!</b>

10:34.400 --> 10:36.240
<b>Surely you know that
as well as anyone!</b>

10:37.240 --> 10:38.490
<b>Miyuki...</b>

10:39.030 --> 10:43.830
<b>Just how it would make me feel...</b>

10:43.830 --> 10:46.580
<b>knowing that you'd been injured...</b>

10:47.000 --> 10:49.790
<b>I'm begging you to please consider that!</b>

10:53.340 --> 10:54.920
<b>I'm sorry.</b>

10:57.300 --> 10:59.010
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
ANCIENT CITY INSURRECTION PART I</b>

10:59.630 --> 11:01.510
<b>OCTOBER 1, A.D. 2096</b>

11:03.680 --> 11:08.020
<b>Today marks the launch
of the 2096 Student Council.</b>

11:09.020 --> 11:10.390
<b>Our vice chairwoman is Izumi.</b>

11:10.940 --> 11:12.400
<b>Our accountant is Honoka.</b>

11:12.730 --> 11:14.400
<b>Our secretary is Minami.</b>

11:14.690 --> 11:17.400
<b>And I, Miyuki Shiba, am your chairwoman.</b>

11:17.860 --> 11:20.910
<b>Also, my brother will be serving
as our chief secretary!</b>

11:21.740 --> 11:25.910
<b>Everyone, I look forward to working
with you in the coming year!</b>

11:26.160 --> 11:29.540
<b>What's with this "chief secretary" thing?
It never existed until now.</b>

11:29.540 --> 11:31.170
<b>You shouldn't go there!</b>

11:31.460 --> 11:32.540
<b>I look forward to it, too!</b>

11:32.830 --> 11:35.420
<b>Getting the chance to serve
on the Student Council with you, Ms. Miyuki,</b>

11:35.420 --> 11:38.550
<b>with your combination of beauty and talent, and
your status as the first student in First High history—</b>

11:38.550 --> 11:41.430
<b>Okay, okay. Let's settle down, all right?</b>

11:41.970 --> 11:44.850
<b>Isn't it great that Tatsuya stayed
on the Student Council?</b>

11:44.850 --> 11:45.850
<b>Yes!</b>

11:47.680 --> 11:49.480
<b>Mikihiko, do you have a second?</b>

11:49.480 --> 11:50.680
<b>What's the matter?</b>

11:50.680 --> 11:52.690
<b>So honored to work with you!</b>

11:53.060 --> 11:54.060
<b>Take a look at this.</b>

11:53.400 --> 11:57.820
<b>I hope we can get closer and closer now!</b>

11:54.810 --> 11:59.320
<b>This is a shikigami's composition,
written onto an activation sequence.</b>

11:59.860 --> 12:01.650
<b>Which brings me to my question.</b>

12:01.650 --> 12:04.280
<b>When it comes to these sequences,
are there any differences in style?</b>

12:04.280 --> 12:05.700
<b>Sure there are.</b>

12:07.580 --> 12:10.700
<b>I think this might be from Shugendo.</b>

12:10.700 --> 12:14.080
<b>What is this?
It's been modified in a weird way.</b>

12:14.500 --> 12:15.630
<b>I see.</b>

12:15.630 --> 12:18.340
<b>Now I get why you were being
so secretive, Tatsuya.</b>

12:18.920 --> 12:22.220
<b>You got this data
from an underground site, right?</b>

12:22.510 --> 12:23.840
<b>Why do you think that?</b>

12:24.340 --> 12:28.810
<b>Because this shikigami
is so obviously for covert surveillance.</b>

12:28.810 --> 12:33.480
<b>I see. So, it was something dangerous.
I'm glad I consulted you.</b>

12:34.020 --> 12:36.480
<b>I'm going to delete this data.</b>

12:37.900 --> 12:40.030
<b>Sorry to be calling so late at night.</b>

12:40.030 --> 12:42.610
<b>Mr. Hayama, is my aunt there?</b>

12:43.280 --> 12:47.740
<b><i>Master Tatsuya, I'm very sorry,
but this isn't a good time for Madam Yotsuba.</i></b>

12:48.370 --> 12:54.120
<b>In that case, may I ask you to convey something
to my aunt about her request for a mission?</b>

12:54.120 --> 12:55.620
<b><i>I'll be glad to.</i></b>

12:56.130 --> 13:00.800
<b>For this job, I'd like to ask the Kudou Family
for their help in searching for the target.</b>

13:00.800 --> 13:06.140
<b>I've already gone through the Fujibayashi Family
to secure a meeting with the Kudou's previous head.</b>

13:06.140 --> 13:06.760
<b><i>Ah...</i></b>

13:07.390 --> 13:09.850
<b><i>So, you've decided to ask
for the help of General Kudou...</i></b>

13:09.850 --> 13:13.020
<b><i>rather than the Independent
Magic-Equipped Battalion?</i></b>

13:13.520 --> 13:18.520
<b>I felt that it'd be wise to avoid becoming
indebted to the JDF over a Yotsuba task.</b>

13:18.940 --> 13:21.650
<b><i>But it's all right to become
indebted to the Kudous?</i></b>

13:22.190 --> 13:26.280
<b>It's highly likely that this Zhou person
has joined forces with the Traditionalists.</b>

13:26.280 --> 13:30.410
<b>In which case, the best strategy
would be to get help from Nine,</b>

13:30.410 --> 13:32.910
<b>which has long been hostile
to the Traditionalists.</b>

13:33.450 --> 13:34.540
<b><i>Hmm.</i></b>

13:34.540 --> 13:38.790
<b>Not only that, but the Kudous owe me
for what happened last month.</b>

13:39.170 --> 13:41.340
<b>Whether they owe us or we owe them...</b>

13:41.340 --> 13:44.420
<b>if it continues for an extended time,
we'll never be able to escape each other,</b>

13:44.420 --> 13:47.680
<b>so I thought we should settle up
before that happens.</b>

13:48.970 --> 13:51.010
<b><i>Despite your youth, Master Tatsuya...</i></b>

13:51.010 --> 13:53.850
<b><i>you're certainly well-versed
in the subtleties of the world.</i></b>

13:53.850 --> 13:57.390
<b><i>Fine, I will relay that to Madam Yotsuba.</i></b>

13:57.390 --> 13:58.810
<b>I'd appreciate that.</b>

13:59.440 --> 14:00.650
<b><i>By the way...</i></b>

14:00.650 --> 14:05.190
<b><i>there's no need to report each time
you plan on obtaining someone's cooperation.</i></b>

14:06.070 --> 14:12.280
<b><i>Madam has said that she'll be leaving
this matter to your discretion.</i></b>

14:18.830 --> 14:21.960
<b>Madam, you heard what he said.</b>

14:24.920 --> 14:26.880
<b>Forgive me, Mr. Hayama!</b>

14:26.880 --> 14:32.140
<b>It's just that what Tatsuya said was so adorable
that I couldn't help myself!</b>

14:32.720 --> 14:36.770
<b>I don't believe
what Master Tatsuya said is wrong.</b>

14:37.310 --> 14:40.650
<b>On the surface, he's correct,
but it's not normal.</b>

14:40.650 --> 14:46.650
<b>Normally, it's through owing and being owed
that you build and deepen bonds.</b>

14:47.240 --> 14:52.030
<b>Master Tatsuya must not feel the need
for connections arising from such debts.</b>

14:53.580 --> 14:55.540
<b>How young he is.</b>

14:57.160 --> 14:59.040
<b>OCTOBER 5, A.D. 2096</b>

14:59.620 --> 15:01.540
<b>I've been wondering about this...</b>

15:02.040 --> 15:05.300
<b>but what is my role
as chief secretary, exactly?</b>

15:06.050 --> 15:11.090
<b>I cannot bear to place you
in a position lower than mine, Brother.</b>

15:11.090 --> 15:15.930
<b>I want you to be above me
even if only in name!</b>

15:16.930 --> 15:18.180
<b>Is that right?</b>

15:39.160 --> 15:43.580
<b><i>They made the synthetic spirit self-destruct,
and scattered the noise of the Psions.</i></b>

15:43.580 --> 15:46.880
<b><i>I guess you could call it
a magical smoke screen.</i></b>

15:46.880 --> 15:48.090
<b><i>Then, the next move will be...</i></b>

15:49.840 --> 15:51.630
<b>Minami! Use Descending Whirlwind!</b>

15:51.630 --> 15:52.840
<b>R-Right!</b>

15:53.430 --> 15:54.930
<b>Whoa! What's going on?</b>

16:03.400 --> 16:04.860
<b>Modern Magic?</b>

16:20.250 --> 16:23.170
<b>No one told us
they'd be using Modern Magic!</b>

16:24.380 --> 16:25.580
<b>I won't let you escape.</b>

16:40.770 --> 16:43.730
<b>There shouldn't be any lasting effects from this.</b>

16:44.310 --> 16:46.440
<b>You've upped your game, Miyuki.</b>

16:46.440 --> 16:48.610
<b>Thank you very much!</b>

16:53.570 --> 16:55.110
<b>About that pair just now...</b>

16:55.490 --> 16:57.990
<b>there's no question
that they were Ancient Magic users.</b>

16:58.370 --> 17:02.750
<b>The spell one of them used to escape
was Sensory Interference Magic,</b>

17:02.750 --> 17:04.750
<b>which makes it hard
for others to identify you.</b>

17:05.040 --> 17:09.210
<b>It's the same type of spell Retsu Kudou used
at the opening ceremony...</b>

17:09.210 --> 17:10.880
<b>for last year's Nine Schools Competition.</b>

17:10.880 --> 17:13.510
<b>Meaning that they work for the Kudous?</b>

17:13.840 --> 17:19.140
<b>No, according to Fumiya,
the Kudous have no reason to attack us.</b>

17:19.140 --> 17:20.760
<b>They must work for the Traditionalists.</b>

17:21.430 --> 17:24.190
<b>We learned two things from today's assault.</b>

17:24.520 --> 17:29.020
<b>First, the fact that we're clearly
being targeted by the Traditionalists.</b>

17:30.610 --> 17:34.150
<b>The other is that the enemy
doesn't know who we are.</b>

17:34.990 --> 17:39.410
<b>This is backed up by the fact
that they thought we were Ancient Magic users.</b>

17:39.950 --> 17:43.790
<b>The enemy almost certainly followed
Fumiya and Ayako here.</b>

17:43.790 --> 17:46.870
<b>They must know that Fumiya
and Ayako are Kurobas...</b>

17:46.870 --> 17:51.210
<b>and that the Kurobas are in charge
of the Yotsubas' work.</b>

17:51.590 --> 17:56.800
<b>But despite knowing that much, they don't know
how they're linked to us and the Yotsubas.</b>

17:56.800 --> 18:01.760
<b>They don't even see us
as magicians serving the Yotsubas.</b>

18:03.100 --> 18:04.140
<b>Meaning...</b>

18:04.480 --> 18:09.770
<b>that they think we're Ancient Magic users
employed by the Kuroba Family?</b>

18:10.110 --> 18:14.610
<b>The enemy may know of our existence,
but they don't know who we really are.</b>

18:14.610 --> 18:18.530
<b>They have no idea why we were chosen
as the Kurobas' collaborators.</b>

18:19.110 --> 18:20.530
<b>In other words...</b>

18:20.990 --> 18:26.710
<b>there's a possibility that the enemy
might attack people other than us?</b>

18:28.120 --> 18:32.800
<b>Shouldn't we put in a request to our aunt
or Mr. Kuroba for protection?</b>

18:33.420 --> 18:36.090
<b>Let's not rely on Aunt Maya.</b>

18:36.090 --> 18:38.180
<b>Then, Master Yakumo?</b>

18:38.720 --> 18:42.850
<b>I have a feeling it's going to cost us...
but we have no choice, do we?</b>

18:45.770 --> 18:50.150
<b>It seems like you've been dragged
into more trouble, huh?</b>

18:50.150 --> 18:51.190
<b>So, you knew?</b>

18:51.730 --> 18:53.820
<b>Mind if I ask you what it's about?</b>

18:54.230 --> 18:56.900
<b>I've accepted a job in the Kyoto area...</b>

18:57.240 --> 18:59.780
<b>and actually, I have a favor to ask of you
regarding this matter.</b>

19:00.280 --> 19:02.580
<b>There's no need to be shy.</b>

19:02.580 --> 19:05.790
<b>I do have some history
with the Traditionalists after all.</b>

19:06.120 --> 19:10.920
<b>So, the branch of Ancient Magic users known
as "the Traditionalists" are involved after all?</b>

19:11.330 --> 19:16.050
<b>They're not known as "the Traditionalists."
That's just what they call themselves.</b>

19:16.050 --> 19:17.760
<b>So, what is this favor you have in mind?</b>

19:18.300 --> 19:24.510
<b>Right. The enemy seems to have mistaken us
for Ancient Magic users hired by the Kurobas.</b>

19:24.510 --> 19:30.020
<b>Which means that they could launch
an attack on my friends.</b>

19:30.270 --> 19:34.770
<b>I see. So, you'd like me
to protect your friends, right?</b>

19:35.270 --> 19:37.650
<b>Yes. Would you be willing to do so?</b>

19:38.190 --> 19:39.860
<b>Sure.</b>

19:39.860 --> 19:44.370
<b>If you want, I'd also be glad to lend you
a hand with that job of yours, too.</b>

19:44.780 --> 19:49.000
<b>No, I couldn't ask you
to help me out with that, Master.</b>

19:49.000 --> 19:53.000
<b>Internal strife between Ancient Magic users
wouldn't be a good look.</b>

19:53.500 --> 19:55.130
<b>Well, well...</b>

19:55.130 --> 19:58.510
<b>It seems like I'm still a long way
from achieving satori.</b>

21:24.630 --> 21:26.010
<b>OCTOBER 6, A.D. 2096</b>

21:26.590 --> 21:28.260
<b>I have something to tell you all.</b>

21:29.140 --> 21:33.140
<b>Yesterday, after we left the station,
someone attacked us.</b>

21:33.560 --> 21:36.150
<b>Oh no! You weren't hurt, were you?</b>

21:36.690 --> 21:37.940
<b>Don't worry.</b>

21:37.940 --> 21:42.530
<b>Neither Brother nor Minami nor I
sustained even a scratch.</b>

21:42.530 --> 21:46.030
<b>That said, we don't know the backstory
of why we were attacked.</b>

21:46.360 --> 21:48.910
<b>You don't even know who the perps were?</b>

21:49.410 --> 21:54.250
<b>The police are looking into it, but all they know
is that they're Ancient Magic users.</b>

21:54.910 --> 21:58.290
<b>So, it's not as if it was
a personal attack on Tatsuya,</b>

21:58.290 --> 22:02.000
<b>but rather, there's a possibility
that they're targeting First High students?</b>

22:02.630 --> 22:05.880
<b>Should we bolster the protection detail
for the Thesis Competition?</b>

22:06.300 --> 22:10.970
<b>The upperclassmen have sufficient protection,
so they should be fine.</b>

22:11.510 --> 22:15.060
<b>I'm more worried about all of you.</b>

22:15.060 --> 22:18.980
<b>Since you're the ones I'm closest to
at First High School.</b>

22:19.440 --> 22:21.070
<b>If that's the story...</b>

22:21.070 --> 22:23.780
<b>Honoka, come over to my place
starting today.</b>

22:23.780 --> 22:25.570
<b>Okay, I'll do that.</b>

22:25.570 --> 22:27.320
<b>I'll be fine.</b>

22:27.320 --> 22:28.950
<b>Needless to say, Miki, too.</b>

22:29.530 --> 22:31.620
<b>You'll be all right, too, won't you?</b>

22:31.620 --> 22:32.540
<b>Well, yeah.</b>

22:33.120 --> 22:35.660
<b>The one I'm worried about is Mizuki.</b>

22:36.210 --> 22:39.540
<b>Tatsuya, I'll be looking after Mizuki
for the time being!</b>

22:40.080 --> 22:42.550
<b>No, our opponents are Ancient Magic users.</b>

22:42.550 --> 22:45.510
<b>We have no idea what kind
of methods they'll use.</b>

22:45.840 --> 22:48.550
<b>It'll be hard enough
just to protect yourself.</b>

22:48.550 --> 22:50.430
<b>But to do that
while also guarding Mizuki...</b>

22:50.430 --> 22:52.760
<b>you wouldn't be a good match for that, Erika.</b>

22:54.680 --> 22:57.520
<b>Okay, then, Miki, you stay with her!</b>

22:57.520 --> 22:59.310
<b>My name is Mikihiko—</b>

22:59.310 --> 23:00.900
<b>Wait, what?</b>

23:00.900 --> 23:03.440
<b>Good idea. Mikihiko, can I count on you?</b>

23:04.070 --> 23:05.480
<b>Um...</b>

23:05.480 --> 23:07.190
<b>Is that okay, Ms. Shibata?</b>

23:07.820 --> 23:11.530
<b>Yes. As long as you're okay with it,
Mr. Yoshida, then please do so.</b>

23:11.530 --> 23:14.950
<b>All right. No matter what happens,
I'll protect you, okay?</b>

23:15.490 --> 23:17.960
<b>All right! I'm counting on you!</b>

23:18.830 --> 23:22.590
<b>We need to go to Nara to take care of something,
so our hands will be tied this weekend.</b>

23:23.170 --> 23:26.460
<b>I'm sorry for the inconvenience,
but all of you, stay safe.</b>

23:36.390 --> 23:40.020
<b>THE IRREGULAR
AT MAGIC HIGH SCHOOL
ANCIENT CITY INSURRECTION PART II</b>
